# Manually transcribed by OWID from three chapters of the volume:
#   - Colombia, p. 95, Table 2, "Working children (12-14 years) as a percentage of all children
#     (12-14 years)". Note the same page carries a Table 1 giving working children as a share of
#     the economically active population (boys 3.2 / 4.8 / 5.7) -- a different measure, not used here.
#   - Japan, p. 80: children in the workforce in Yamanashi prefecture (1879) and nationally (1920).
#   - Spain, p. 62, Table 3, "Activity rates in Sabadell's textile industry, by age and gender,
#     1857-1858", the 8-15 row. Recorded here under 1857.
# Verified against the book on 2026-09-06: the Colombia and Sabadell figures match exactly. The
# Japan figures have NOT yet been checked against p. 80.
# In case of updating, upload manually.

# Learn more at:
# http://docs.owid.io/projects/etl/architecture/metadata/reference/
meta:
  origin:
    # Data product / Snapshot
    title: "Child labour in historical perspective (1800-1985)"
    description: |-
      A collection of case studies of child labor in Europe, Japan and Colombia, published by the UNICEF International Child Development Centre. The chapters draw on population censuses and other national and local records to measure how common children's work was and how it declined.

      The figures taken from this volume here are the share of children of a given age recorded as working or as having an occupation, in Colombia nationally, in Yamanashi prefecture and Japan, and in the textile industry of Sabadell in Catalonia.
    date_published: "1996"

    # Citation
    producer: Cunningham and Viazzo
    citation_full: |-
      Cunningham, H., & Viazzo, P. P. (Eds.) (1996). Child labour in historical perspective, 1800-1985: Case studies from Europe, Japan and Colombia (pp. 62, 80, 95). UNICEF International Child Development Centre / Istituto degli Innocenti, Florence, Italy.
    attribution_short: UNICEF

    # Files
    url_main: https://ideas.repec.org/p/ucf/hisper/hisper96-1.html
    date_accessed: '2026-09-06'

    # License
    license:
      name: CC BY 4.0
      url: https://ideas.repec.org/p/ucf/hisper/hisper96-1.html
